44:32.502 --> 44:35.763
[SPEAKER_01]: You were a tuku of Sheshan Khyentsev as well, right?

44:36.043 --> 44:42.044
[SPEAKER_00]: There is some, there is a little bit of a story that maybe I can tell you.

44:42.824 --> 44:49.326
[SPEAKER_00]: That in Khyentse Rinpoche's dream, I was recognized by Karmapa, so I'll tell you the secret also.

44:49.766 --> 45:00.448
[SPEAKER_00]: Khyentse Rinpoche went, after Karmapa told him that, Khyentse Rinpoche one time went to Nama Buddha and he had a dream of the three main masters of Sheshan, Khyentse Rinpoche, Ramchandra Rinpoche and Kongtrul Rinpoche.

45:01.868 --> 45:07.753
[SPEAKER_00]: And then they had some exchange discussions through some kind of poem.

45:08.893 --> 45:16.779
[SPEAKER_00]: And mainly Rinpoche was saying that he felt very sad that you all died in the Cultural Revolution in Tibet.

45:18.040 --> 45:25.984
[SPEAKER_00]: So somehow they all sort of merge into one and dissolve into kind of being a reincarnation.

45:26.825 --> 45:33.868
[SPEAKER_00]: So then the Karmapa and Khyentse Rinpoche and Chojulingpa in Rumtheg, they had a discussion, what to name me.

45:37.670 --> 45:45.813
[SPEAKER_00]: So, Khyentse Rinpoche wanted to give me the name of Sheshen Khyentse because he was more close to him.

45:46.773 --> 45:54.236
[SPEAKER_00]: And Chojol Lingpa asked, who is the most important Lama from Sheshen?

45:54.376 --> 45:56.797
[SPEAKER_00]: And Chojol Lingpa said, that's Sheshen Ramja.

45:57.657 --> 46:01.759
[SPEAKER_00]: So then Chojol Lingpa said, okay, if there's a choice, let's go for the highest.

46:05.140 --> 46:05.500
[SPEAKER_00]: So then,

46:07.500 --> 46:11.342
[SPEAKER_00]: My grandmother later told Ujjain Dhamcharambache, don't tell this story.

46:11.882 --> 46:15.603
[SPEAKER_00]: The people will say that Khyentse Dhamcharambache made his own nephew a tukku.

46:15.763 --> 46:16.904
[SPEAKER_00]: So just leave it.

46:17.104 --> 46:17.764
[SPEAKER_00]: Karmapa did it.

46:17.784 --> 46:18.764
[SPEAKER_00]: His own grandson.

46:18.804 --> 46:20.245
[SPEAKER_00]: His own grandson as a tukku.

46:20.605 --> 46:24.306
[SPEAKER_00]: So just don't talk about this thing because people cannot accept these days, you know.

46:24.386 --> 46:25.107
[SPEAKER_00]: They make rumors.

46:25.447 --> 46:26.667
[SPEAKER_00]: So just leave it, Karmapa.

46:27.367 --> 46:29.228
[SPEAKER_00]: So somehow they're all three involved.

46:31.389 --> 46:31.589
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

46:32.270 --> 46:38.154
[SPEAKER_00]: So just now, my name is Ram Jam, successor of Sheshan Ram Jam.

46:40.115 --> 46:44.959
[SPEAKER_01]: And so the previous, Sheshan Gil Sab was a teacher of Khyentse Rinpoche.

46:44.979 --> 46:48.121
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, teacher of Khyentse Rinpoche and direct student of Mipham Rinpoche.

46:48.421 --> 46:50.002
[SPEAKER_01]: A direct student of Mipham Rinpoche.

46:50.022 --> 46:50.883
[SPEAKER_01]: Amazing.

46:50.983 --> 46:51.963
[SPEAKER_00]: This is amazing, right?

46:52.003 --> 46:55.666
[SPEAKER_00]: And unfinished Mipham Rinpoche's works as hand robot.

46:55.726 --> 46:57.147
[SPEAKER_01]: And he has that responsibility.

46:59.715 --> 47:00.895
[SPEAKER_01]: That's quite a responsibility.

47:01.375 --> 47:01.656
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

47:02.176 --> 47:07.137
[SPEAKER_01]: So did Khyentse Rinpoche tell you any stories about Sheshen Gyatsov that you remember?

47:07.717 --> 47:11.898
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, he would never even name, call Sheshen Gyatsov.

47:11.918 --> 47:13.178
[SPEAKER_00]: He would just say the kindness one.

47:13.819 --> 47:13.899
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh.

47:14.499 --> 47:17.039
[SPEAKER_00]: So when he says kindness one, it's Sheshen Gyatsov.

47:17.140 --> 47:17.460
[SPEAKER_00]: Wow.

47:18.200 --> 47:26.822
[SPEAKER_00]: I've never seen Khyentse Rinpoche cry except when visiting the Sheshen Gyatsov's retreat when we were in Tibet.

47:28.604 --> 47:29.926
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'm very, very close.

47:29.966 --> 47:34.813
[SPEAKER_01]: So now you're concentrating on doing retreat and passing on the lungs.

47:35.053 --> 47:36.435
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it, yes.

47:36.716 --> 47:38.378
[SPEAKER_00]: Then I enjoy myself sometimes.

47:38.418 --> 47:40.261
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything else?

47:42.284 --> 47:44.345
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything else you want to share?

47:44.625 --> 47:46.286
[SPEAKER_01]: I want to be conscious of your time as well.

47:46.326 --> 47:46.666
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

47:46.886 --> 47:51.948
[SPEAKER_00]: I think one thing, maybe one unique quality of Khyentse Rinpoche is, like I said, non-sectarian.

47:52.528 --> 47:55.390
